	(text "${d684d2fa-09c2-4534-8acf-a2a601e81a10:REFERENCE}" (at 326.71 249.604592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "319c8ea0-063f-50f5-bb88-2aaa13214f9a"))
	(text "PLACE: ${d684d2fa-09c2-4534-8acf-a2a601e81a10:REFERENCE} in the middle of the block between the input and output edges, ${18be2134-0c6d-468e-977a-6ec186e213ba:REFERENCE}" (at 321.63 254.684592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6dde5216-78d4-5d4e-9dba-06487cbbc86f"))
	(text "hard against pin 5 with a short return to pin 2; +3.3V and GND reach the block through" (at 321.63 257.224592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f05451d0-d12c-57c4-abbd-6f8a8b09b874"))
	(text "vias." (at 321.63 259.764592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c9fa181d-affc-58b7-9070-bf894992b079"))
	(text "ROUTE: +3.3V carries PWR_3V3_LOCAL; the block's baseline is 0.2 mm tracks and 0.6/0.3" (at 321.63 263.574592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "402b8fe9-b167-5fe9-b8b8-2f8f4ecabe7a"))
	(text "mm vias." (at 321.63 266.114592 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ac4a264d-9fd5-548d-b5b8-e77a521e95ae"))
	(text "INTERFACES" (at 423.76 36.482 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "605a3a45-14dd-5de9-9121-91eab8c565f8"))
	(text "Buffer supply (VCC, pin 5), 1.65 to 5.5 V; always-on when the taps must be observable before firmware runs, switched when the consumer of" (at 423.76 46.99 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "49fd3785-a22f-543b-9115-7d8447725d0e"))
	(text "IN_A/IN_B powers down with it (Ioff keeps the unpowered outputs off the bus)." (at 423.76 49.53 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b6f65e14-66a7-532c-8cc3-98e4284c1f60"))
	(text "Return for the buffer (pin 2), both filter capacitors and the four pull-downs." (at 423.76 59.69 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b3a4849e-bf19-515e-afd8-cf2aeaec4615"))
	(text "Field-wired channel A input, 0 to 5.5 V legal at any VCC; pulled low by ${99885ad5-2487-4f42-b5fc-c7884fa6dbc3:REFERENCE} (100 k) when unplugged." (at 423.76 72.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "854224d1-59f5-5900-8726-43fcc1f8c8be"))
	(text "Field-wired channel B input, 0 to 5.5 V legal at any VCC; pulled low by ${f3b8ada3-8efc-416a-99a3-6e33fba471fa:REFERENCE} (100 k) when unplugged." (at 423.76 85.09 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fb268c0f-5d11-5a26-bb38-8d9be7910492"))
	(text "Conditioned channel A, 3.3 V logic from 1Y (pin 6); pulled down by ${2810be90-e8c8-4226-8b89-017f00ae77cb:REFERENCE} when the rail is off." (at 423.76 97.79 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8c925618-e41b-5c64-bc1e-88cea5a50807"))
	(text "Conditioned channel B, 3.3 V logic from 2Y (pin 4); pulled down by ${b5415b67-1b92-49cb-991a-c122d10e2357:REFERENCE} when the rail is off." (at 423.76 110.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "44df8f71-f333-5d29-a522-2a06ddc43c4b"))
	(text "Instrument tap of IN_A through ${485f934b-7a2f-4f64-8b94-d6f4ebd9e779:REFERENCE} (100 ohm), INSTRUMENT class." (at 423.76 123.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "03fc509b-55ce-5440-aed1-c6501d694e9d"))
	(text "Instrument tap of IN_B through ${10c9ffe1-aac2-4e2f-a89b-02c2fadf5966:REFERENCE} (100 ohm), INSTRUMENT class." (at 423.76 135.89 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "121f9755-e2a2-5a49-8ffb-41576c059ffd"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 423.76 151.13) (xy 578.76 151.13)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "c3e614e6-bab0-59f1-87a7-0a3a774b50d8"))
	(text "OPERATION" (at 423.76 153.67 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "77376c3c-2e29-53d3-a70a-1f7004d77610"))
	(text "Signal path, per channel: IN_A_RAW -> ${504d6ccc-f8c0-42f9-837f-e30ebb7dd752:REFERENCE} (4.7 k) -> IN_A_FILT (${5e0c81c3-f412-4c13-8485-ec7f1d59d7d1:REFERENCE} 470 pF to GND) -> ${d684d2fa-09c2-4534-8acf-a2a601e81a10:REFERENCE} 1A (pin 1) -> 1Y (pin 6) -> IN_A," (at 423.76 157.82 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "39ce7c99-bf33-5bf5-8eac-d2779bc89834"))
	(text "tapped through ${485f934b-7a2f-4f64-8b94-d6f4ebd9e779:REFERENCE} (100 ohm) to IN_A_INST; channel B is ${cd916f99-47ea-446c-b1ea-7b65d79d30fd:REFERENCE}, ${7103dcd1-83f6-4991-a1ac-6565d56e2e67:REFERENCE}, 2A (pin 3), 2Y (pin 4), IN_B and ${10c9ffe1-aac2-4e2f-a89b-02c2fadf5966:REFERENCE} to IN_B_INST." (at 423.76 160.36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "12ced2cb-8689-5179-90db-6e1fbc76e017"))
	(text "${99885ad5-2487-4f42-b5fc-c7884fa6dbc3:REFERENCE}/${f3b8ada3-8efc-416a-99a3-6e33fba471fa:REFERENCE} (100 k) pull the raw inputs low when unplugged, on the harness side of the series resistor so no divider eats VIH margin;" (at 423.76 162.9 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "26fbaa94-e9af-5f83-ac54-1b1eee266346"))
	(text "${2810be90-e8c8-4226-8b89-017f00ae77cb:REFERENCE}/${b5415b67-1b92-49cb-991a-c122d10e2357:REFERENCE} (100 k) define the outputs when +3.3V is off." (at 423.76 165.44 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3e2e7fce-958d-50a3-b8ca-067214a38d2c"))
	(text "Filter: 4.7 k and 470 pF give a time constant of about 2.2 us and a corner near 72 kHz; a 3.3 V edge reaches the worst-case VT+ of 2.0 V about 2" (at 423.76 169.25 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d2044491-e126-505c-a46b-bcf72ce5039e"))
	(text "us later, the same on both channels, so relative timing is kept. For faster edges swap ${5e0c81c3-f412-4c13-8485-ec7f1d59d7d1:REFERENCE}/${7103dcd1-83f6-4991-a1ac-6565d56e2e67:REFERENCE} (27 pF gives about 1.25 MHz)." (at 423.76 171.79 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cb5d4916-b2e9-5fa4-868d-684a834dd937"))
	(text "The Schmitt input is the point: at VCC = 3 V, VT+ is 1.3 to 2.0 V and VT- 0.8 to 1.3 V with at least 0.4 V of hysteresis, so slow or noisy field edges" (at 423.76 175.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d5cff748-124f-5855-adab-36c2dfe99989"))
	(text "cannot double-trigger; a 3.3 V source clears VT+ by at least 1.3 V, a 5 V TTL VOH of 2.4 V by 0.4 V. Inputs are rated 0 to 5.5 V at any VCC (6.5 V" (at 423.76 178.14 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ebf01e2b-a9f3-54e5-ae13-cd5d4ff97b04"))
	(text "absolute), so a 5 V source is legal; a source below ground draws about 0.2 mA per volt through the 4.7 k (about 1 mA from -5 V), and a short to 36" (at 423.76 180.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1b51b1e7-1fb3-5dbb-9194-95654ea0356e"))
	(text "V is bounded to about 7 mA into the buffer." (at 423.76 183.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "27881559-4383-55f3-aabc-4e5a5494ef43"))
	(text "Supply: VCC 1.65 to 5.5 V, 10 uA max, +/-24 mA drive at 3 V; Ioff (10 uA max) keeps the outputs off a live downstream input when the rail is down," (at 423.76 187.03 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "679277e6-9f34-5db1-8f9c-f12d3e5065e2"))
	(text "which is why the sequencing between source and buffer does not matter. ${18be2134-0c6d-468e-977a-6ec186e213ba:REFERENCE} (100 nF) bypasses pin 5." (at 423.76 189.57 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "14c6960e-5d46-52ee-8cd4-9a184bd494c3"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 423.76 201) (xy 578.76 201)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "42de625d-c774-555a-a2e7-b574abb908ef"))
	(text "DESIGN CONTRACT" (at 423.76 203.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d85070ed-1a95-57e7-8fa7-c6770751259b"))
	(text "Two-channel single-ended logic input conditioner: per-channel series/RC filtering plus an SN74LVC2G17 dual Schmitt-trigger buffer that turns a 3.3" (at 423.76 207.69 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d68fabd5-2f1f-53ce-9529-1a5f1074675c"))
	(text "V or 5 V field-wired logic signal into clean 3.3 V logic, with a 100 ohm InstrumentPort tap on each output. Generic sibling of" (at 423.76 210.23 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6e8395ad-05fd-5ab6-9515-817630122124"))
	(text "quadrature_encoder_input_5v_sn74lvc2g17: same circuit and values, generic names, no encoder-supply passthrough. Use this one for BNC trigger and" (at 423.76 212.77 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e131a76d-7595-52d4-85f1-300d6c4ebcb6"))
	(text "sync inputs, sensor and switch logic lines and any other pair of inputs a board conditions; use the encoder block when the harness also carries the" (at 423.76 215.31 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d9e3f77b-7cad-5bb9-8f4d-be1ba5867412"))
	(text "encoder supply; place this block twice for four inputs. Connector-agnostic: the jack or terminal lives on the board sheet. Bring the raw lines in on" (at 423.76 217.85 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "756c39b8-8cff-5026-8fc2-182efd9b6315"))
	(text "IN_A_RAW and IN_B_RAW, take conditioned 3.3 V logic out on IN_A and IN_B and the taps out on IN_A_INST and IN_B_INST; rails +3.3V and GND." (at 423.76 220.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "af0c014b-0178-5dfb-ad70-3cef71dadadf"))
	(text "Per channel: ${504d6ccc-f8c0-42f9-837f-e30ebb7dd752:REFERENCE}/${cd916f99-47ea-446c-b1ea-7b65d79d30fd:REFERENCE} 4.7 kohm series (OW-RES-4K7-0402, C25900) into ${5e0c81c3-f412-4c13-8485-ec7f1d59d7d1:REFERENCE}/${7103dcd1-83f6-4991-a1ac-6565d56e2e67:REFERENCE} 470 pF C0G to ground" (at 423.76 222.93 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0ec4d437-3eee-5fd4-8d94-bcdcd22640a0"))
	(text "(OW-CAP-470P-0402-C0G-100V, C1518202) and ${d684d2fa-09c2-4534-8acf-a2a601e81a10:REFERENCE} SN74LVC2G17DRYR gate A/B (OW-MISC-SN74LVC2G17DRYR, C2675856);" (at 423.76 225.47 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "95265088-3214-5014-940e-39feaa6427f4"))
	(text "${99885ad5-2487-4f42-b5fc-c7884fa6dbc3:REFERENCE}/${f3b8ada3-8efc-416a-99a3-6e33fba471fa:REFERENCE} 100 kohm pull-down (OW-PASS-RC0402JR-07100KL, C106234) on the harness side of the series resistor, so an unplugged input" (at 423.76 228.01 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "067e49f5-5390-5694-947d-63b5331fa164"))
	(text "reads low without forming a divider that eats VIH margin; ${2810be90-e8c8-4226-8b89-017f00ae77cb:REFERENCE}/${b5415b67-1b92-49cb-991a-c122d10e2357:REFERENCE} 100 kohm pull-down on each output for Ioff high-Z, so an always-on" (at 423.76 230.55 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "657c04b5-85be-5fb6-a13b-57ac27b96399"))
	(text "downstream buffer never sees a floating input when this rail is down; ${485f934b-7a2f-4f64-8b94-d6f4ebd9e779:REFERENCE}/${10c9ffe1-aac2-4e2f-a89b-02c2fadf5966:REFERENCE} 100 ohm T-taps (OW-PASS-0402WGF1000TCE, C25076) to" (at 423.76 233.09 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b6c15a2f-8345-5817-8327-92621ec736d2"))
	(text "the _INST ports, INSTRUMENT netclass from the instrument-taps profile; ${18be2134-0c6d-468e-977a-6ec186e213ba:REFERENCE} 100 nF (OW-CAP-100N-0402-X5R-16V, C162178) hard against" (at 423.76 235.63 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "61c40d56-2c89-58e6-8a98-f46159aa993e"))
	(text "${abd6e6d8-65ef-4922-8cec-490a1d04449e:REFERENCE} pin 5." (at 423.76 238.17 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "06755355-d83d-5906-9d00-e8eb76ffcc38"))
	(text "The Schmitt input is the point of the block: an ordinary LVC buffer specifies a maximum input transition rate of about 8 ns/V, which a slow or noisy" (at 423.76 240.71 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5249dd09-734b-5ccc-a9d7-25dca29e96bc"))
	(text "field edge violates and double-triggers; the 2G17 has no such limit and 0.4 V minimum hysteresis at 3 V. Thresholds VT+ <= 2.0 V and VT- >= 0.8" (at 423.76 243.25 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "bc7690ed-a7a9-5a6e-906b-7885a7e59627"))
	(text "V, so a 3.3 V microcontroller pin clears the high threshold by 0.9 V or more and a 5 V TTL-level VOH of 2.4 V by 0.4 V." (at 423.76 245.79 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f075f267-cfea-55d0-9696-fe11181ce609"))
	(text "Tolerance: inputs are rated 0 to 5.5 V at any valid VCC, 6.5 V absolute maximum, with no clamp diode to VCC, so a 5 V source plugged in by mistake" (at 423.76 248.33 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "802fc482-9887-5a9f-b968-7508dea90adc"))
	(text "is legal; a source held below ground draws about 0.2 mA per volt through the 4.7 kohm (a -5 V DAC output about 1 mA), and a short to a 36 V rail" (at 423.76 250.87 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3b090451-4fec-58cd-b0f7-6096b52f18db"))
	(text "is bounded to about 7 mA and destroys a 0.19 USD buffer instead of the consumer." (at 423.76 253.41 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1a17018e-3b1b-53cb-a290-e085b3b8c134"))
	(text "Filter: 4.7 kohm and 470 pF give a 72 kHz corner and about 2 us from a 3.3 V edge to the Schmitt threshold, the same on both channels so their" (at 423.76 255.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fd022e4e-33d1-567d-af99-8a2db8a0d080"))
	(text "relative timing is preserved; 470 pF suits sub-10 kHz timing edges on long unshielded leads, swap ${5e0c81c3-f412-4c13-8485-ec7f1d59d7d1:REFERENCE}/${7103dcd1-83f6-4991-a1ac-6565d56e2e67:REFERENCE} for a faster corner when the" (at 423.76 258.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a80bb9f6-d9fe-5011-8cf9-5aef3c66a81d"))
	(text "signal needs it (27 pF gives 1.25 MHz)." (at 423.76 261.03 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cc5a68f2-c052-530b-bcd6-b043af28700a"))
	(text "Rails are generic labels: bind +3.3V to the always-on rail when the taps must be observable before firmware runs, or to the switched domain when" (at 423.76 263.57 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1bb85dea-60ab-53ef-858a-9a6cb0559bb5"))
	(text "the consumer of IN_A/IN_B can be powered down and must rise and fall with it; sequencing between source and buffer is a non-issue because Ioff" (at 423.76 266.11 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cce499ca-215b-5c7b-9750-851fdb6cdf89"))
	(text "disables the outputs when the part is unpowered." (at 423.76 268.65 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "37ecc925-6699-5649-beb7-b14c4c656d09"))
	(text "First consumer: camera-gpio-interface-pcb, TRIG IN and SYNC IN BNCs from a pyControl breakout on IN_A_RAW/IN_B_RAW, TRIG_IN/SYNC_IN out, taps" (at 423.76 271.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5e137003-ce32-58f2-b7be-abc7b45f97f7"))
	(text "on DIG0/DIG1 of the digital-50 InstrumentPort." (at 423.76 273.73 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fd1395e9-89f6-5d48-959b-ca7289133561"))
	(text "Series resistors and filter capacitors on the input edge, the 2G17 and its decoupling in the middle, output pull-downs and taps on the output edge," (at 423.76 276.27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "23cff065-faee-5f55-aa52-10baa8b0ca49"))
	(text "so harness-side nets stay on one edge and logic and tap nets leave on the other. Keep the input pair away from motor bridge outputs and give it a" (at 423.76 278.81 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2470f3a2-8af3-5a3c-96bf-2de2d5bcb7fc"))
	(text "ground reference." (at 423.76 281.35 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f28d0e4d-123a-5e30-b05b-32df4f5e15db"))
	(text "Project-local pending bench verification; promotable once a second board uses it." (at 423.76 283.89 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "eac52f6b-46cc-5bb8-82a6-caa503c2088f"))
